# Pilot contact channel. Optional — the app ships with baked-in defaults
# (tranth3truong@gmail.com / +84827745579), so the footer link and lead form
# work without any env config. Set these only to override per deployment.
# VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT posts leads as JSON; without it the form opens a mailto.
VITE_LEAD_ENDPOINT=
VITE_LEAD_EMAIL=tranth3truong@gmail.com
VITE_LEAD_PHONE=+84827745579
# API origin for HTTP calls. Leave EMPTY on Vercel: vercel.json rewrites /api/*
# to the Space, so the browser calls its own origin and no CORS allow-list can
# take the site down when the domain changes (see DEC-0021). Leave empty too for
# local dev and for the combined HF Space build, which serves this site itself.
# Set an absolute HTTPS origin only when pointing a local dev server at a remote
# API on purpose.
VITE_API_BASE=
# Websocket origin. A Vercel rewrite will not carry an upgrade to an external
# host, so /ws/* always goes direct and needs an absolute HTTPS origin whenever
# VITE_API_BASE is empty on a Vercel deployment. Falls back to VITE_API_BASE,
# then to the page origin (correct for the combined Space build).
# Vercel production: https://tranth3truong-carepath-api.hf.space
VITE_WS_BASE=
# VITE_CONSOLE_URL was dropped with the interpreter console: it pointed at
# /phien-dich-y-khoa/, which is now a deliberate 404.
